      "notes": [
        "Every animal noun is capitalised — that is not a typo, all German nouns are.",
        "Learn the article with the word: <b>der</b> Hund, <b>die</b> Katze, <b>das</b> Pferd. Gender is what most learners get wrong.",
        "<b>das Tier</b> (animal) is the general word; <b>das Haustier</b> is a pet.",
        "The plural of most animals here adds -e or -en: der Hund → die Hunde, die Katze → die Katzen.",
        "A few stay identical in the plural: der Hamster → die Hamster, das Zebra → die Zebras."
      ]
    },
